{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>My El, my El</b> — twice, because he was in distress." "And the sense of <b>my El</b> — because of 'you have forsaken me,' and the word 'my El' is lacking, as if he says: My El is far from my salvation; these are the words of my roar, like the roar of my groaning heart. And he added 'words,' because he is a human being."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:06.788148406Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}